{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016Wc9emAcyLLHD27Bf7pcqA","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\"command\":\"story-verify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"revise\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"dcbc4543-77eb-48ca-ae16-47342b85f1a1\",\"role\":\"story_verifier\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.5\",\"sessionId\":\"019ec517-957e-7520-99ad-8c58c7c12cc1\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"codex\",\"sessionId\":\"019ec517-957e-7520-99ad-8c58c7c12cc1\",\"storyId\":\"02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation\"},\"mode\":\"initial\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation\",\"title\":\"Story 2: Event Capture and Turn Derivation\"},\"artifactsRead\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/stories/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation.md\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/test-plan.md\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/converter.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/runtime-changes.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/turn-accumulator.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/state.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/turn-derivation.test.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/abort.test.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/idempotency.test.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/support.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/package.json\",\"manual node reproduction: resume/reload idempotency collision using built packages/pi-lhc/dist/index.js\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Initial verification covered Story 2 AC/TC requirements, Flow 2 tech design, capture/runtime production paths, Story 2 tests, configured gates, and manual existing-thread reattach scenarios.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[],\"newFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-001\",\"severity\":\"critical\",\"title\":\"Existing-thread resume/reload can silently skip new finalized events\",\"evidence\":\"AC-2.1 requires every finalized PI message to be recorded exactly once, and AC-2.6/TC-2.7 require duplicate safety without normal-resume historical replay. On every session_start, createConnector resets captureSession.sourceSeq to 0 in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:310-318; nextEntryId then returns s0, s1, ... in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:352-357; message/runtime hooks use that generated entryId in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:362-384. eventKey gives entryId first precedence in packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts:35-40, so a fresh connector attached to an existing thread reuses prior keys. Manual reproduction against the built production connector: after recording user_prompt 'first', starting a fresh connector with --session for the same thread and recording user_prompt 'second after resume', intakeStream.listEvents returned only the first event with key pi:th_947f6dd71f50d513:entry:s0:0:user_prompt and connector diag was null. The same reload shape returned only the first event with key pi:th_d1fc3d71df1144d3:entry:s0:0:user_prompt. Existing TC-2.7 coverage in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts:108-153 only proves identical batch re-delivery skips; it does not prove normal resume/reload continues recording new events.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/idempotency.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.1\",\"AC-2.6\",\"AC-2.7\",\"TC-2.7\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-001\",\"severity\":\"critical\",\"title\":\"Existing-thread resume/reload can silently skip new finalized events\",\"evidence\":\"AC-2.1 requires every finalized PI message to be recorded exactly once, and AC-2.6/TC-2.7 require duplicate safety without normal-resume historical replay. On every session_start, createConnector resets captureSession.sourceSeq to 0 in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:310-318; nextEntryId then returns s0, s1, ... in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:352-357; message/runtime hooks use that generated entryId in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:362-384. eventKey gives entryId first precedence in packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts:35-40, so a fresh connector attached to an existing thread reuses prior keys. Manual reproduction against the built production connector: after recording user_prompt 'first', starting a fresh connector with --session for the same thread and recording user_prompt 'second after resume', intakeStream.listEvents returned only the first event with key pi:th_947f6dd71f50d513:entry:s0:0:user_prompt and connector diag was null. The same reload shape returned only the first event with key pi:th_d1fc3d71df1144d3:entry:s0:0:user_prompt. Existing TC-2.7 coverage in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts:108-153 only proves identical batch re-delivery skips; it does not prove normal resume/reload continues recording new events.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/idempotency.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.1\",\"AC-2.6\",\"AC-2.7\",\"TC-2.7\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"TC-2.1 happy-path ordered user/assistant/toolResult capture and assistant thinking/text/tool_call fan-out\",\"AC-2.2\",\"TC-2.2\",\"TC-2.3\",\"AC-2.3\",\"TC-2.4\",\"AC-2.4\",\"TC-2.5\",\"AC-2.5\",\"TC-2.6\",\"AC-2.8\",\"TC-2.9\",\"TC-2.8 explicit malformed-event/store-unavailable failure isolation\",\"Idempotency architecture-risk double-replay for identical batches\"],\"unverified\":[\"AC-2.1 across existing-thread resume/reload\",\"AC-2.6 for normal resume/reload continuation after prior captures\",\"AC-2.7 for false duplicate-skip capture loss\",\"TC-2.7 normal resume does not replay historical messages while new messages still record\"]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"manual node --input-type=module existing-thread resume/reload idempotency reproduction\",\"result\":\"fail\"}],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"Production capture path uses real LHC intakeStream.messageEvents, but reattach state is not durable: sourceSeq and turn_end closedCount reset for every fresh connector, making new events on existing threads collide with prior idempotency keys.\",\"No material fake/mock intake path was found in Story 2 capture modules; test fakes are confined to fixtures and explicit test SDK config.\"],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"revise\",\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"openQuestions\":[],\"additionalObservations\":[\"Configured gates passed with 54 tests, but the current suite does not cover the existing-thread resume/reload collision path.\"]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/004-verify.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-14T07:45:17.544Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-14T07:49:35.833Z\"}\n2\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4562dd99-e915-4997-a6b6-c06f59211979","uuid":"a9574205-5f9f-4c2f-a6e8-bc3e68df074b","timestamp":"2026-06-14T07:49:55.128Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/004-verify.json","content":"{\"command\":\"story-verify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"revise\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"dcbc4543-77eb-48ca-ae16-47342b85f1a1\",\"role\":\"story_verifier\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.5\",\"sessionId\":\"019ec517-957e-7520-99ad-8c58c7c12cc1\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"codex\",\"sessionId\":\"019ec517-957e-7520-99ad-8c58c7c12cc1\",\"storyId\":\"02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation\"},\"mode\":\"initial\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation\",\"title\":\"Story 2: Event Capture and Turn Derivation\"},\"artifactsRead\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/stories/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation.md\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/test-plan.md\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/s