{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011yKxa4D435DKRdsgAdQ9qP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All gates green: 58 tests pass, `test-immutability` OK (8 frozen files: 2 lifecycle + 5 original capture + 1 new reattach), `verify-all` clean. SV-001 is fixed, the new tests objectively catch the bug (proven via the temporary revert), and duplicate-safe re-delivery is preserved.\n\n{\n  \"outcome\": \"ready-for-verification\",\n  \"planSummary\": \"Fixed verifier finding SV-001 (critical): existing-thread resume/reload silently skipped new finalized events because captureSession.sourceSeq and the accumulator's turn counter restarted at 0 on every fresh connector, and the entryId tier of the idempotency key ignores content — so a resumed session's new events reused prior keys (s0, turn:0, ...) and were deduped away (AC-2.1/AC-2.6 violation). Root cause: the synthesized entry index was process-local, not durable. Fix: at session_start the connector now SEEDS its capture counters from the thread's durable committed state (inspect.overview events.count → sourceSeq, turns.closed → accumulator startTurnSeq), one touch-suppressed read per attach. A resume/reload continues numbering past every prior key; a brand-new thread reads back zero and is byte-for-byte unchanged; the converter's same-key dedup (the reload/crash-replay/deterministic-replay safety net) is untouched because that path delivers identical keys, while live sessions number forward. Added a 4-case regression suite and proved it catches the bug (reverting the seed makes cases 1–3 fail with the exact skip/collision the verifier reproduced) and that the fix passes. All configured gates green; 8 Red-phase files frozen (the new suite included).\",\n  \"changedFiles\": [\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\", \"reason\": \"session_start now seeds captureSession.sourceSeq and the accumulator's startTurnSeq from the thread's durable committed state via built.value.sdk.inspect.overview(threadRef) (events.count / turns.closed), so a fresh connector on an existing thread continues past the prior session's idempotency keys instead of restarting at 0; falls back to 0 on an unreadable overview (new/unavailable thread). Updated the stale CaptureSession / nextEntryId comments.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/turn-accumulator.ts\", \"reason\": \"Added an optional startTurnSeq to TurnAccumulatorCtx (default 0) seeding closedCount, so a reattached session's turn_end keys continue past the prior session's turn:N keys rather than colliding at turn:0; default-0 keeps the frozen accumulator goldens and all fresh-thread tests unchanged.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts\", \"reason\": \"NEW — SV-001 regression suite: (1) fresh connector resuming an existing thread records a new event (not skipped); (2) reload does the same; (3) normal resume records new messages and does not duplicate prior history, with two distinct closed turns (proving turn_end keys also continue); (4) re-flushing an identical batch through the converter is still skipped (duplicate-safe re-delivery preserved). Verified to fail on the pre-fix code and pass after.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/support.ts\", \"reason\": \"Added attachCapture(store, launch, reason) to drive a fresh connector onto an existing thread (e.g. { session: threadId } with reason resume/reload); startCapture now delegates to it with identical behavior, so the frozen tests are unaffected.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/test/red-manifest.json\", \"reason\": \"Recorded the new reattach-idempotency regression test so the Green-exit immutability guard protects it.\" }\n  ],\n  \"tests\": {\n    \"added\": [\n      \"test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts (4 cases: resume-records-new, reload-records-new, resume-no-duplicate-history, duplicate-safe re-delivery)\",\n      \"test/capture/support.ts attachCapture helper (assertion-free scaffolding)\"\n    ],\n    \"modified\": [\n      \"test/capture/support.ts (startCapture delegates to attachCapture)\",\n      \"test/red-manifest.json (recorded the new regression test)\"\n    ],\n    \"removed\": [],\n    \"totalAfterStory\": 58,\n    \"deltaFromPriorBaseline\": 25\n  },\n  \"gatesRun\": [\n    { \"command\": \"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify -- test/capture\", \"result\": \"pass\" },\n    { \"command\": \"pnpm --filter pi-lhc green-verify\", \"result\": \"pass\" },\n    { \"command\": \"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all\", \"result\": \"pass\" }\n  ],\n  \"selfReview\": {\n    \"findingsFixed\": [\n      \"SV-001: existing-thread resume/reload no longer collides new finalized events with prior idempotency keys — capture counters are seeded from durable thread state at attach. Proven by reverting the seed (cases 1–3 fail with exactly the skip the verifier reproduced: ['first'] instead of ['first','second...']) and re-applying (all pass).\",\n      \"Turn-boundary leg of the same bug: turn_end keys also restarted at turn:0 on reattach and would skip the resumed turn's close; the accumulator's seedable startTurnSeq fixes it (case 3 asserts two distinct closed turns).\",\n      \"Confirmed the fix is non-regressive: all fresh-thread tests read back count 0 → seed 0 → identical keys/behavior; the converter's same-key dedup path is unchanged (case 4 + the original TC-2.7 and corpus double-replay stay green).\"\n    ],\n    \"findingsSurfaced\": [\n      \"The seed read falls back to 0 when inspect.overview is not ok; on a genuinely-existing-but-unreadable thread that could theoretically reintroduce a collision, but an unreadable overview means the store is unavailable/new and capture would itself fail to a gap/health signal — no silent double-record.\",\n      \"Within-session re-delivery dedup lives at the converter (identical keys), not the connector: the connector treats each message_end as a distinct finalization and numbers it forward, which matches the AC-2.6 re-delivery paths (reload/crash-replay = fresh process; deterministic replay) rather than a hypothetical within-process double-fire of the same message.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"openQuestions\": [\n    \"Story 3's deterministic replay (verify/replay.ts) must seed from 0 for a from-scratch corpus so a re-replay re-derives identical keys and dedups (AC-6.2); it should NOT route through the connector's seed-from-count session path. Flagged for Story 3.\",\n    \"The durable-count seeding assumes resume/reload do not re-fire COMMITTED history (verified for resume, §5a). When PI's real per-entry id is exposed on the message_end hook, it should key events directly (the highest idempotency tier), making the synthesized index unnecessary and covering any future re-fire-committed-history shape. Carried from the initial story payload.\"\n  ],\n  \"specDeviations\": [\n    \"Capture idempotency counters (source-event index and turn counter) are seeded from the thread's durable committed-event and closed-turn counts at session_start — a capture-scoped, touch-suppressed read added to the composition root to make resume/reload continuation safe (SV-001). This refines the initial implementation's process-local counters; the converter.capture() signature and the eventKey precedence are unchanged.\",\n    \"Carried from the initial payload: the aborted-turn corpus fixture includes the abort runtime_note; map→accumulate orchestration lives in the index.ts composition root (capture surface may not import lifecycle); TurnAccumulator has a constructor; eventKey optionals are widened to '?: T | undefined'; the connector synthesizes the entry index because PI's real entry id is not in the declared hook slice yet.\"\n  ],\n  \"recommendedNextStep\": \"Re-run story-verify to confirm SV-001 is closed (the new reattach-idempotency suite plus the existing 54 cover AC-2.1/AC-2.6/AC-2.7/TC-2.7 across resume/reload), then proceed to Story 3 (Capture Verification), ensuring its replay harness seeds keys deterministically from scratch rather than through the connector's seed-from-count path.\"\n}"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":457,"cache_read_input_tokens":396847,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":457},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4562dd99-e915-4997-a6b6-c06f59211979","uuid":"f81cc6bc-3816-4263-a3f7-34085ec5762d","request_id":"req_011Cc2oX8LvtLoyQmdPbSm5e"}
